module

public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.ReesGradedAlgebraEpiDegree
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.ConormalAlgebraSquareMapAmbientComparison

/-!
# Propagation of surjectivity of the ambient comparison of a square to every degree

Let a commutative square of algebraic spaces over a scheme `S` be given, together with an
ambient homomorphism `Ψ` as in [Stacks Project, Tag 09RS], and let

`χ : g^*(⨁_{n ≥ 0} (𝓘')ⁿ) ⟶ ⨁_{n ≥ 0} 𝓘ⁿ`

be the ambient comparison `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.conormalAlgebraSquareAmbientComparison` that
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Spaces/ConormalAlgebraSquareMapAmbientComparison.lean` builds out
of them.  Its target is the Rees graded algebra of the kernel ideal sheaf of `i`, so
`SheafOfModules.epi_unitalHom_app_of_nonneg` applies to it: **if `χ` carries the unit and is
surjective in the degrees zero and one, it is surjective in every nonnegative degree.**
Composing with the factorisation of the canonical map of Stacks 09RS gives the same for
the canonical map.

The mathematical content is in `SheafOfModules.epi_unitalHom_app_of_nonneg`, whose own input is
the local surjectivity of multiplication of the Rees graded algebra: `𝓘^{i + j}` is locally
generated by products of sections of `𝓘ⁱ` and `𝓘ʲ`.  This file is the instantiation of that
induction at the ambient comparison of a square, and the identification of the two spellings of
the structure sheaf of rings of an algebraic space it needs.

## Relation to [Stacks Project, Tag 09RT]

Stacks 09RT asserts that the canonical map of Stacks 09RS is surjective when the square is
cartesian and `i`, `i'` are immersions, and an isomorphism when moreover `g` is flat.  The
surjectivity assertion is
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.epi_conormalAlgebraSquareMapOfPullbackHom_app_of_nonneg` below, which
carries the Stacks 09RT attribute for that clause; the isomorphism assertion is
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isIso_conormalAlgebraSquareMapOfPullbackHom_app_of_isFlat` in
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Spaces/ConormalAlgebraSquareMapFlatClause.lean`.  The two together
are the tag's covering set.

What this file adds to the reduction already recorded in
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Spaces/ConormalAlgebraSquareMapAmbientComparison.lean` is the
degree induction: there, surjectivity of the canonical map in a degree was deduced from
surjectivity of the ambient comparison *in that same degree*; here surjectivity in *every*
nonnegative degree is deduced from surjectivity in the degrees zero and one.

### What is carried, and why it is a disclosure and not the conclusion

**The square being cartesian is not consumed**, and neither is either vertical arrow being an
immersion.  In the source the cartesian hypothesis acts only through the degree-one statement,
and the degree-one statement is carried.  Three inputs are carried.

Neither the cartesian hypothesis nor the immersion hypotheses appear below, not even as unused
parameters: as in
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Spaces/ConormalAlgebraSquareMapAmbientComparison.lean`, the
statements are for an arbitrary commutative square and arbitrary vertical arrows, so they are
strictly more general than the situation of Stacks 09RT and specialise to it.

* `hunit`, that `χ` carries the degree-zero unit.  This is a property of `Ψ` and the conclusion
  of no named result: `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.conormalAlgebraSquareMapOfPullbackHom` takes `Ψ`
  as an *arbitrary* parameter, and at `Ψ = 0` the comparison carries the unit only if the unit of
  the target is zero.  A canonical `Ψ` is what would discharge it, and the module documentation
  of the ambient-comparison file records what constructing one still needs.
* `h0`, surjectivity of `χ` in degree zero.  In degree zero the ambient comparison is the map
  `g^*𝒪_{X'} ⟶ 𝒪_X` of structure sheaves, and this is the conclusion of
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.epi_structureSheafMap`, transported to this square.
* `h1`, surjectivity of `χ` in degree one.  In degree one the ambient comparison is the map
  `g^*(𝓘') ⟶ 𝓘` of ideal sheaves, and this is the conclusion of
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.epi_idealSheafMap`, transported to this square.

`h1` is **[Stacks Project, Tag 04CQ]'s conclusion and not 09RT's**.  The degree-one part of the
canonical map of Stacks 09RS is the canonical map of conormal *modules* of
[Stacks Project, Tag 04CP], and 04CQ is the statement that that map is surjective; 04CQ is proved
and separately tagged, in
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Spaces/ConormalModuleBaseChangeEpi.lean` and — in the reduced form
"surjectivity, reduced to surjectivity of the map of defining ideal sheaves", which is exactly
the shape carried here — in
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Spaces/ConormalModuleFlatBaseChange.lean`.  Carrying a
differently-tagged proved result at a particular instance discloses an input; carrying 09RT's own
conclusion in degree one would instead restate the conclusion, and that is not what happens here.

The transport is itself part of what `h0` and `h1` carry.  The two degree-one results are stated
for the canonical preimage square of a **closed** subspace —
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.preimageSubspace` with
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.preimageProjection` and
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.conormalEtaleRestrictionSquare` — whereas Stacks 09RT has an abstract
cartesian square whose vertical arrows are **immersions**.  Two identifications are needed for
the passage, and **only the second is missing**.

The first, that `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.kernelIdealSheaf` of the inclusion of a cartesian square
is the defining ideal sheaf of the preimage subspace, *is* available, also outside the étale case.
It is
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.kernelIdealSheaf_eq_definingIdealSheaf_preimageSubspace_of_isPullback`
of `StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Spaces/ConormalModuleBaseChangeCartesian.lean`, and it needs
nothing new: the kernel ideal sheaf of the inclusion of a closed subspace is that subspace's
defining ideal sheaf by definition
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.kernelIdealSheaf_eq_definingIdealSheaf`), and a cartesian square
presents its upper subspace as the inverse image on the nose
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.closedSubspaces_eq_preimageSubspace_of_isPullback`).

The second, the degree-one agreement of
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.kernelIdealSheafZPowPullbackMap` with
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.idealSheafMap`, **is also in**:
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.kernelIdealSquareMap_one_eq_idealSheafMap` of
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Spaces/KernelIdealSquareMapDegreeOne.lean`.  It is stated for
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.kernelIdealSquareMap`, of which that ambient map is the second factor,
because the ambient map alone has no source in common with
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.idealSheafMap`.

The route is not the chartwise one this note expected.  Rather than comparing the two chartwise
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.ModuleFMap`s given by `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.chartDiagramPullback`
and passing from that to the equality of the transposed morphisms, both maps are taken at their
composite with the inclusion of the sheaf of ideals into the structure sheaf —
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.idealSheafMap_comp_definingIdealSheaf_ι` and
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.kernelIdealSquareMap_comp_ι`, whose right-hand sides are the same term
once the two sheaves of ideals are identified — and that inclusion is a monomorphism.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.epi_conormalAlgebraSquareAmbientComparison_app_of_nonneg`: **the
  ambient comparison of a square is surjective in every nonnegative degree as soon as it carries
  the unit and is surjective in the degrees zero and one.**
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.epi_conormalAlgebraSquareMapOfPullbackHom_app_of_nonneg`: **the
  surjectivity clause of [Stacks Project, Tag 09RT]** for the canonical map of
  [Stacks Project, Tag 09RS], by the factorisation.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.structureRingSheaf_eq_tensorSheafificationStructureSheaf`: the two
  spellings of the structure sheaf of rings of an algebraic space agree.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 09RS](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/09RS)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 09RT](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/09RT)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0FQW](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0FQW)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 04CQ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/04CQ)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory
open Stacks.Sheaves.GradedAlgebraEssentiallySmall (gradedPull)

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Space

variable (B : BigFppfSite.{u}) (S : Scheme.{u}) (hS : B.Contains S)

/-- **The structure sheaf of rings of an algebraic space is the structure sheaf of a ringed site
in the sense of `Stacks.SheafOfModules.TensorSheafification`**: both are the structure sheaf of
commutative rings with commutativity forgotten, packaged with the transported sheaf condition. -/
theorem structureRingSheaf_eq_tensorSheafificationStructureSheaf (W : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS) :
    Stacks.SheafOfModules.TensorSheafification.structureSheaf
        (structureSheaf B S hS W.1 W.2).obj (structureRingSheaf B S hS W).property =
      structureRingSheaf B S hS W :=
  rfl

variable {Z X X' Z' : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS}

/-- **The sheaf of graded algebras `⨁_{n ≥ 0} 𝓘ⁿ` of the kernel ideal sheaf of a morphism is the
Rees graded algebra of that sheaf of ideals on the ringed site of the target.**  Both sides are
`SheafOfModules.reesGradedAlgebra` at the same sheaf of ideals; the commutativity arguments
differ, and are proofs of the same proposition. -/
theorem kernelIdealGradedAlgebra_eq_reesGradedAlgebraOfRingedSite
    {Y : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS} (p : X ⟶ Y) :
    kernelIdealGradedAlgebra B S hS p =
      SheafOfModules.reesGradedAlgebraOfRingedSite (structureRingSheaf B S hS Y).property
        (kernelIdealSheaf B S hS p) :=
  rfl

/-- **The ambient comparison of a commutative square is surjective in every nonnegative degree
as soon as it carries the unit and is surjective in the degrees zero and one.**

Its target is the Rees graded algebra of the kernel ideal sheaf of `i`, whose multiplication is
locally surjective in every pair of nonnegative degrees
(`SheafOfModules.isLocallySurjective_reesMulPresheaf`), so the degree induction of
`SheafOfModules.epi_unitalHom_app_of_nonneg` applies: a local section of `𝓘^{n + 1}` is locally
a sum of products of a section of `𝓘ⁿ` and a section of `𝓘`, and both factors are locally in
the image.

This is not the surjectivity assertion of [Stacks Project, Tag 09RT]: the degrees zero and one
are hypotheses, and they are where the source consumes the square being cartesian.  The module
documentation records what discharging them needs. -/
theorem epi_conormalAlgebraSquareAmbientComparison_app_of_nonneg (i : Z ⟶ X) (i' : Z' ⟶ X')
    (f : Z ⟶ Z') (g : X ⟶ X')
    (Ψ : (gradedPull (X := smallEtaleRingedTopos B S hS X)
          (Y := smallEtaleRingedTopos B S hS X') (smallEtaleRingedToposHom B S hS g)).obj
        (kernelIdealGradedAlgebra B S hS (f ≫ i')) ⟶ kernelIdealGradedAlgebra B S hS i)
    (hunit : SheafOfModules.sectionsMap
        ((conormalAlgebraSquareAmbientComparison B S hS i i' f g Ψ).app 0)
        ((gradedPull (X := smallEtaleRingedTopos B S hS X)
            (Y := smallEtaleRingedTopos B S hS X')
            (smallEtaleRingedToposHom B S hS g)).obj
          (kernelIdealGradedAlgebra B S hS i')).one =
      (kernelIdealGradedAlgebra B S hS i).one)
    (h0 : Epi ((conormalAlgebraSquareAmbientComparison B S hS i i' f g Ψ).app 0))
    (h1 : Epi ((conormalAlgebraSquareAmbientComparison B S hS i i' f g Ψ).app 1))
    (n : ℤ) (hn : 0 ≤ n) :
    Epi ((conormalAlgebraSquareAmbientComparison B S hS i i' f g Ψ).app n) :=
  SheafOfModules.epi_unitalHom_app_of_nonneg (structureRingSheaf B S hS X).property
    (kernelIdealSheaf B S hS i)
    (SheafOfModules.GradedAlgebra.UnitalHom.ofHom
      (conormalAlgebraSquareAmbientComparison B S hS i i' f g Ψ) hunit) h0 h1 n hn

/-- **The surjectivity clause of [Stacks Project, Tag 09RT].**  The canonical map
`f^*𝒞_{Z'/X',*} ⟶ 𝒞_{Z/X,*}` of [Stacks Project, Tag 09RS] is surjective in every nonnegative
degree.

The ambient comparison is surjective in every nonnegative degree by
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.epi_conormalAlgebraSquareAmbientComparison_app_of_nonneg`, and the
canonical map is in each degree the inverse image along `i` of the ambient comparison preceded by
two isomorphisms.

Three inputs are carried: that the ambient comparison carries the unit, and its surjectivity in
the degrees zero and one — the conclusions of
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.epi_structureSheafMap` and of
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.epi_idealSheafMap`, the ideal-sheaf form of
[Stacks Project, Tag 04CQ]'s surjectivity clause, transported to this square.  The square being
cartesian is therefore not consumed, and neither is either vertical arrow being an immersion.
What is proved is that the three suffice: surjectivity propagates from the degrees zero and one
to every degree.  The module documentation says why none of the three is available in the
library, and why carrying the degree-one one is carrying 04CQ's conclusion and not this tag's. -/
@[stacks 09RT "the surjectivity clause, in every nonnegative degree; the cartesian hypothesis is \
NOT consumed, three inputs being carried: hunit, h0 and h1, the degree-one one being Tag 04CQ's \
surjectivity clause in ideal-sheaf form transported to this square; the flat clause is \
isIso_conormalAlgebraSquareMapOfPullbackHom_app_of_isFlat"]
theorem epi_conormalAlgebraSquareMapOfPullbackHom_app_of_nonneg (i : Z ⟶ X) (i' : Z' ⟶ X')
    (f : Z ⟶ Z') (g : X ⟶ X') (hsq : i ≫ g = f ≫ i')
    (Ψ : (gradedPull (X := smallEtaleRingedTopos B S hS X)
          (Y := smallEtaleRingedTopos B S hS X') (smallEtaleRingedToposHom B S hS g)).obj
        (kernelIdealGradedAlgebra B S hS (f ≫ i')) ⟶ kernelIdealGradedAlgebra B S hS i)
    (hunit : SheafOfModules.sectionsMap
        ((conormalAlgebraSquareAmbientComparison B S hS i i' f g Ψ).app 0)
        ((gradedPull (X := smallEtaleRingedTopos B S hS X)
            (Y := smallEtaleRingedTopos B S hS X')
            (smallEtaleRingedToposHom B S hS g)).obj
          (kernelIdealGradedAlgebra B S hS i')).one =
      (kernelIdealGradedAlgebra B S hS i).one)
    (h0 : Epi ((conormalAlgebraSquareAmbientComparison B S hS i i' f g Ψ).app 0))
    (h1 : Epi ((conormalAlgebraSquareAmbientComparison B S hS i i' f g Ψ).app 1))
    (n : ℤ) (hn : 0 ≤ n) :
    Epi ((conormalAlgebraSquareMapOfPullbackHom B S hS i i' f g hsq Ψ).app n) :=
  epi_conormalAlgebraSquareMapOfPullbackHom_app_of_epi_ambientComparison B S hS i i' f g hsq Ψ n
    (epi_conormalAlgebraSquareAmbientComparison_app_of_nonneg B S hS i i' f g Ψ hunit h0 h1 n hn)

end AlgebraicGeometry.Space

end
